Supporting Documents

This folder contains supporting documents that showcase my professional background, aptitude, and career development. It will continue to be updated with relevant files from my past experience, current learning journey, and future achievements as I transition into a Business Analyst role.

Files Included

* Shadow Match – Personal Evaluation Report

This document contains the results of a comprehensive psychometric and aptitude assessment conducted by Shadow Match, a talent assessment and organizational development company based in Pretoria, South Africa.

The assessment provides insight into my cognitive abilities, behavioural preferences, problem-solving approach, communication style, and workplace strengths. As part of my professional portfolio, it demonstrates qualities that are valuable in analytical and business-focused roles, including critical thinking, attention to detail, adaptability, structured decision-making, and continuous learning.

The report serves as an independent evaluation of my potential to contribute effectively in data-driven and business analysis environments.

* Recommendation Letter – Hostings 101

This recommendation letter confirms my employment with Hostings 101, a Pretoria-based company specializing in Search Engine Optimization (SEO), web hosting, and website design, where I served as a Project Coordinator and Systems Maintenance & SEO Trainee.

In this role, I coordinated project activities, assisted with systems maintenance, and collaborated with a small technical team and external consultants to support the successful delivery of client and internal projects. The position provided practical experience in structured workflows, process coordination, stakeholder communication, problem-solving, and the interaction between business requirements and technical implementation.

As part of my professional development, I also completed certification in Graphics and Website Design to gain a deeper understanding of web technologies and digital solutions. While my career aspirations lie in business analysis rather than software development, this technical foundation enables me to communicate effectively with technical teams, understand system functionality, and bridge the gap between business needs and technology.

The experience strengthened my organizational, analytical, and cross-functional collaboration skills, providing a strong foundation for my transition into a Business Analyst career.
